WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.035 --> 00:00:15.115
looked around the table.

2
00:00:16.436 --> 00:00:18.297
There were many place settings.

3
00:00:18.957 --> 00:00:23.720
But the only ones at the table were the Hatter, the March Hare, and the Dormouse.

4
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.361
"Why are there so many dishes?"

5
00:00:26.822 --> 00:00:27.942
Alice asked the Hatter.

6
00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:34.245
"It's always six o'clock, so that means it's always time for tea," he explained.

7
00:00:34.265 --> 00:00:37.167
"We don't have time to wash the dishes."

8
00:00:37.187 --> 00:00:42.869
"So when you need clean dishes, you move to the next place setting?"

9
00:00:43.329 --> 00:00:44.070
Alice asked.

10
00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.851
The Hatter nodded in agreement.

11
00:00:46.871 --> 00:00:51.093
"Exactly." Alice thought about this for a moment.

12
00:00:56.495 --> 00:00:58.576
what happens when you come back to where you started?"

13
00:01:01.768 --> 00:01:04.849
"Let's change the subject," the March Hare said.

14
00:01:04.869 --> 00:01:07.030
"I'm getting bored.

15
00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.691
I think the young lady should tell us a story."

16
00:01:09.711 --> 00:01:12.893
"What?" Alice shook her head.

17
00:01:12.913 --> 00:01:15.594
"But I don't know any stories."

18
00:01:15.614 --> 00:01:21.876
"Then the Dormouse will tell us one," the March Hare and the Hatter said together.

19
00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:27.058
They pinched the Dormouse on both sides at once.

20
00:01:29.559 --> 00:01:31.981
"Tell us a story," the March Hare said.

21
00:01:32.001 --> 00:01:35.043
"Yes, please do," Alice begged.

22
00:01:35.063 --> 00:01:38.446
"And be quick about it.

23
00:01:38.866 --> 00:01:42.049
Or you'll fall asleep before you're done," the Hatter added.

24
00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.532
The Dormouse sat up straight and began to talk.

25
00:01:46.633 --> 00:01:50.416
"Once upon a time, there were three little sisters.

26
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:54.599
Their names were Elsie, Lacie, and Tillie.

27
00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:59.823
They lived at the bottom of a well, and—" "Did they get hungry down there?"

28
00:02:00.123 --> 00:02:00.804
Alice asked.

29
00:02:01.488 --> 00:02:04.989
She was always interested in what people ate and drank.

30
00:02:07.470 --> 00:02:09.291
The Dormouse thought for a moment or two.

31
00:02:12.973 --> 00:02:16.534
lived on molasses," he finally said.

32
00:02:17.655 --> 00:02:19.355
Alice shook her head in disbelief.

33
00:02:19.895 --> 00:02:22.597
"Those girls couldn't have done that," she said gently.

34
00:02:22.617 --> 00:02:24.537
"That would have made them ill."

35
00:02:24.557 --> 00:02:31.060
"Yes, they were very ill," the Dormouse said.

36
00:02:32.464 --> 00:02:35.846
Alice tried to imagine what it would be like to live in a well.

37
00:02:37.026 --> 00:02:37.706
But she couldn't.

38
00:02:37.726 --> 00:02:40.648
"Why did they live at the bottom of a well?"

39
00:02:43.169 --> 00:02:46.310
"Have some more tea," the March Hare said to her.

40
00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:49.451
"I've had nothing so far," Alice said.

41
00:02:49.471 --> 00:02:51.632
"So I can't have more."

42
00:02:51.652 --> 00:02:55.334
"Nonsense!" the March Hare said.

43
00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:59.796
"If you have nothing, anything is more than that."

44
00:03:01.460 --> 00:03:03.142
Alice didn't know what to say to this.

45
00:03:12.109 --> 00:03:15.491
So she helped herself to tea, and bread and butter.

46
00:03:16.372 --> 00:03:19.374
Then she turned to the Dormouse and repeated her question.

47
00:03:19.394 --> 00:03:22.837
"Why did the sisters live at the bottom of a well?"

48
00:03:23.938 --> 00:03:26.540
Again the Dormouse took a few moments to think.

49
00:03:28.096 --> 00:03:31.898
"Because it was a molasses well."

50
00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:34.420
"There's no such thing!"

51
00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:36.241
Alice said angrily.

52
00:03:36.261 --> 00:03:41.224
The Hatter and March Hare shushed her.

53
00:03:42.004 --> 00:03:43.345
The Dormouse frowned.

54
00:03:43.365 --> 00:03:53.051
"If you can't be nice," he said, "you can finish the story yourself."

55
00:03:53.671 --> 00:03:54.932
"No, please go on.

56
00:03:55.508 --> 00:03:58.169
I promise to stay quiet and listen," Alice said.

57
00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:02.250
"I want a clean cup," the Hatter interrupted.

58
00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:10.532
So they all moved one place to the right, and the Dormouse went on with his story.

59
00:04:10.552 --> 00:04:20.695
"The sisters were drawing things beginning with the letter M such as—" "Why with an M?"

60
00:04:21.275 --> 00:04:22.016
Alice asked.

61
00:04:22.036 --> 00:04:26.637
"I don't think—" "Then you shouldn't talk," the Hatter said.

62
00:04:27.938 --> 00:04:31.219
This bit of rudeness was more than Alice could bear.

63
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.181
She got up in disgust.

64
00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:38.383
As she walked away, the Dormouse fell asleep.

65
00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:43.725
The Hatter and the March Hare didn't seem to notice her leaving.

66
00:04:45.386 --> 00:04:48.867
Alice looked back several times, hoping they would call after her.

67
00:04:49.928 --> 00:04:54.471
But now they were busy trying to put the Dormouse into the teapot.

68
00:04:54.491 --> 00:05:00.817
"I'll never go there again," Alice said as she walked through the woods.

69
00:05:00.837 --> 00:05:03.980
"That was the dumbest tea party ever."
